\staccato is not a command that can be executed on its
own. It is highlighted in the editor, but running it
gives an "unknown command" error.

A staccato is written after a note with a hyphen and a
dot, like:

\bar stacc-1 {
    \inst1 c'4-. d'-. e'2
}

A staccato note sounds for a percentage of its duration,
50% by default. To change this percentage, use
\notedur.staccato with an integer from 1 to 100:

\notedur.staccato 40

This is applied to all instruments. See also
\staccatissimo and \tenuto.
